# Directory spec for Continuous Integration. One same-basename file spec per workflow file
# may be added if a pipeline grows substantial behaviour; the jobs stay described here.

Spec: workflows

Platform: GitHub Actions

Purpose:
  Continuous integration for the workspace: it gates every change on tests, formatting, lint,
  and coverage, and publishes container images, the kubectl plugin release, and the docs parity
  check on the right triggers.

Structure:
  ./test.yml: Gate job set — test, fmt, clippy, coverage
  ./agent.yml: Build and publish the agent image on tag
  ./operator.yml: Build and publish the operator image on tag
  ./server.yml: Build and publish the server image on tag
  ./cli.yml: Build and release the kubectl-vynil plugin on tag
  ./docker-agent-test.yml: Build-only smoke of the agent and operator Dockerfiles
  ./docs.yml: English/French documentation parity check
  ../scripts/check-docs-parity.sh: EN/FR parity checker invoked by docs.yml

Owns:
  ./*.yml
  ../scripts/check-docs-parity.sh

Must:
  Run `cargo test`, `cargo fmt --check` on nightly, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`, and a
    `cargo tarpaulin` coverage gate on every push to `main` and every pull request.
  Publish images to both Docker Hub and `ghcr.io` for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` on tag push.
  Build the plugin for `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, and
    `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`, scoping cargo to `kubectl-vynil/Cargo.toml`.
  Build each image from its own crate Dockerfile under `/`.

Must not:
  Gate a change that only touches documentation on the Rust build jobs.
  Publish a mutable tag other than `latest` and the `github.ref_name` tag.

Depends on:
  /agent/Dockerfile.sdd
  /operator/Dockerfile.sdd
  /server/Dockerfile.sdd

Tasks:
  [ ] #0 Get `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` green under the strict harness so the Clippy job can
    stop failing.
  [ ] #1 Keep the pinned Rust toolchain aligned with each Dockerfile `RUST_VERSION`.
